  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` with the island, water, day/night sky and orbiting camera. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it or build it with `vite build`, so I haven't seen a rendered frame and the visuals are untested.\n\n- **Island:** about 2,300 flat-shaded triangles built in code, with vertex colours by height (sand, grass, rock). The coastline is irregular. It has up to 18 low-poly trees (trunk plus two cone crowns, instanced) and up to 12 box rocks near the shore.\n- **Water:** a 240-unit grid with a custom GLSL material. Vertex waves, faceted low-poly shading, a fresnel mix toward the sky colour, white crests, a sun or moon glint, and a fade toward the sky colour in the distance. The wave clock and light and sky colours are updated every frame.\n- **Sky and lighting:** `sky.preetham` with stars, a 20-second cycle and the sun moved on an arc. The sun's intensity and colour change (warm near the horizon), and a moon light and a hemisphere light keep the scene lit at night. `?hour=` freezes the time of day.\n- **Camera:** `camera.orbit` at [21, 12, 23] looking at the island, with `autoRotate` 0.12 rad/s, so it sits above the water and frames the whole island.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the frame after the first `onFrame` callback.\n\nOne risk: the water fades toward a sky colour I estimate in code, so a faint band may show at the horizon where it meets the Preetham sky.\n\n",
